Supplier Policy

    This policy defines the conditions suppliers
must satisfy before they can be selected.

    The company maintains a list of currently
approved suppliers. Approved suppliers should
be preferred when selecting a supplier.

    An unapproved supplier may only be selected
after additional human approval.

    A supplier should provide the requested product
or service, the required quantity, the total price,
the expected delivery time, and warranty information
when applicable.

    The supplier should meet the delivery deadline
specified in the purchase request.

    If a supplier cannot meet the required delivery
deadline, it should normally not be recommended when
another suitable supplier can satisfy the requirement.

    Warranty length should be considered when comparing
suppliers. When suppliers have similar prices and delivery
times, a better warranty may be considered an advantage.

    If the recommended supplier is not currently approved,
human approval is required before the purchase can continue.
